- ACTION: Move the rotated 'Absorbance' title (and its up arrow) further left so it no longer overlaps the 0.2–0.8 tick labels; increase left padding to reserve a clean column for the ticks.
- ACTION: Broaden the right flank of the Gaussian (larger sigma above 215 nm, e.g. ~9–10) so absorbance is still ~0.10 at 240 nm and merges smoothly into the 0.065 tail, matching the source curve shape.
- ACTION: Let the chart fill the available container height (reduce forced bottom whitespace or increase the target plot height) so the figure reads like the full-width source image.
- ACTION: Extend the pink background gradient so a faint tint remains down to about 80% of the plot height, matching the source's slower fade to white.

